1
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,500
Hey, you guys, guess what?

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:06,920
Barry and Mindy are getting a divorce.

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:10,590
What is the matter with you?

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,090
No. Barry and Mindy.

5
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:18,550
Oh, sorry. I hear "divorce," I immediately go to Ross. Heh.

6
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:21,430
Who's Barry and Mindy?

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,940
Barry was the guy I almost married, and Mindy was my best friend.

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,770
Wasn't he cheating on you with her?

9
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:30,400
That just means he was falling asleep on top of her instead of me.

10
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,740
Can you imagine if I'd married him? How different would my life be?

11
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:38,870
I know. I've always wondered how different life would be...

12
00:00:39,030 --> 00:00:40,780
if I'd never gotten divorced.

13
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,910
Which time?

14
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,910
The first time!

15
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:47,170
Imagine if Carol hadn't realized she was a lesbian.

16
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:52,710
I can't. I keep seeing it the good way.

17
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:56,430
I bet I'd still be doing my karate.

18
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:02,770
Towards the end of our marriage, I did karate as a way of releasing the tension...

19
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:06,190
from, you know, not doing anything else physical.

20
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:08,850
Maybe the problem was pronouncing it "ka-ra-tay."

21
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,230
What if I was still fat?

22
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,820
You wouldn't be dating me, that's for sure.

23
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:16,360
Sure I would.

24
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:20,370
What? You guys think I'm that shallow?

25
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:22,280
No, I think Monica was that fat.

26
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:27,960
Hey, imagine if I'd never gotten fired off Days of Our Lives.

27
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,460
Hey. Hey, there's Carol again.

28
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,880
What if I had had the guts to quit my job?

29
00:01:35,050 --> 00:01:38,840
I'd probably be writing for The New Yorker, being paid to be funny.

30
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:42,050
But my job's fun too. I mean, tomorrow...

31
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,220
I don't have to wear a tie.

32
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,850
What if I'd taken that job at Merrill Lynch?

33
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,060
What?

34
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,060
Merrill Lynch?

35
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:54,570
A massage client who worked there said I had a knack for stocks.

36
00:01:54,730 --> 00:01:55,940
Why didn't you take it?

37
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:59,740
At that time, you see, I thought that everything that rhymed was true.

38
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:01,990
So I thought if I worked with stocks...

39
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:06,580
I'd have to live in a box and only eat lox and have a pet fox.

40
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:12,880
Do you think if all those things happened, we'd still hang out?

41
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,590
Oh, my God. Rachel Green?

42
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,970
Aah! Rob Tilman!

43
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:06,350
No, heh, no, it's me. Ross.

44
00:03:06,510 --> 00:03:09,730
Oh, I'm sorry. Ross Tilman.

45
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:15,690
No. No, no. Ross Geller.

46
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:15,690
Of course! Monica's brother.

47
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,530
Yeah. Right.

48
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,530
Wow! How are you?

49
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:23,110
Good. Good, I'm married.

50
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:23,110
Oh! Me too! Ha, ha.

51
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,580
Isn't it the best?

52
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,580
Oh, it's the best. Heh.

53
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:32,660
So, um, how's Monica?

54
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:32,660
Really, really great.

55
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:37,670
Actually, she's right down the street. Um, you should stop by and say hi.

56
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,590
Oh, I would love to.

57
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,590
Yeah, she'd be so excited.

58
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:42,260
Oh, okay.

59
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:42,260
Come on.

60
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:44,180
Wait, don't you have to pay for...

61
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,350
Busty Ladies?

62
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:53,310
No, that's okay. Some kid asked me to pick it up for him, but I...

63
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:05,490
So, Monica, still going out with Dr. Boring, huh?

64
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:09,740
He's not boring. He's just...

65
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:14,080
He's just low-key.

66
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:17,330
Here you go, one hazelnut latte.

67
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:17,330
Thank you.

68
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,170
You know, the hazelnut, actually not a nut.

69
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:23,670
It's a seed.

70
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:25,590
Wow.

71
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:31,220
Can anyone else name a well-known seed that's been masquerading as a nut?

72
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:34,060
Oh, dear God. Let me think.

73
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,650
Hey.

74
00:04:37,190 --> 00:04:38,980
Oh, no. What's the matter?

75
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,690
I got another rejection letter.

76
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:44,440
They said my writing was funny, just not "Archie Comic funny."

77
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:47,740
I gotta get back to the hospital.

78
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:48,950
All right.

79
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:48,950
Okay.

80
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,620
Bye.

81
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,620
Bye-bye.

82
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:55,460
Oh, uh, by the way, the answer is the Brazil nut.

83
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:01,920
Was his question, "What's more boring than him?"

84
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:04,970
Hey, man. Sorry about that Archie thing.

85
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:06,840
You, uh, need me to give you some money?

86
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:10,220
Hey, I may have no money, but I still have my pride.

87
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:12,810
Really?

88
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,850
Eh.

89
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:19,440
Joey doesn't have to give you money.

90
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:22,520
TV stars have assistants, right?

91
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:22,520
That's an idea.

92
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:25,860
If I hire an assistant, would you take money from her?

93
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:29,240
No, Joey. Chandler could be your assistant.

94
00:05:29,490 --> 00:05:31,660
He could answer your fan mail and stuff.

95
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,490
That would be great! Let's do that!

96
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,120
I could use the money. Give me time to write.

97
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:38,080
Great! Welcome aboard.

98
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:38,080
Okay!

99
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:40,500
All right. I need to use the bathroom.

100
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:43,670
Since I don't need assistance in there, take a break!

101
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,210
All right.

102
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,680
Hey.

103
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,680
Hey, Phoebe.

104
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:49,840
Guess what?

105
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:49,840
What?

106
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,600
Joey just hired Chandler.

107
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,390
Oh, that's so sweet.

108
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,390
Oh! Hang on!

109
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,890
Hang on!

110
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,360
Go!

111
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:06,440
No. No, no. I said sell when it hits 50!

112
00:06:06,690 --> 00:06:10,280
Five-oh! It's a number! It comes after four-nine!

113
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:14,450
No, it's okay. It's okay. You're allowed one mistake.

114
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,750
Just kidding. You are of course fired.

115
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,370
Ugh.

116
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,670
Hey, Mon?

117
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,670
Hey.

118
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:23,840
Mon, look who I ran into.

119
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:26,630
Oh, my God, Rachel!

120
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:33,390
God, you look terrific!

121
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:33,390
Oh, so do you!

122
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:34,890
Thanks.

123
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:38,350
Did you lose weight?

124
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:38,350
You are so sweet to notice.

125
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,190
Yes, I lost 3 and a half pounds.

126
00:06:40,350 --> 00:06:41,560
Ah!

127
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,820
You remember my friend Chandler?

128
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,820
Hi.

129
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,190
And that's Phoebe.

130
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,190
Hi.

131
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:52,990
Sit down. Sit down. How long's it been since we've seen each other?

132
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:56,910
1987, the day after Christmas. Uh, Sean McMahan's party.

133
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:01,620
I played you one of my songs. "Interplanetary Courtship Ritual."

134
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:05,790
Oh, yeah. Right.

135
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:09,340
So, now, do you still do music?

136
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:09,340
Well, sometimes.

137
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:12,180
Sometime I'll play you...

138
00:07:09,590 --> 00:07:12,180
Oh, my God!

139
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:17,720
Joey Tribbiani from Days of Our Lives just walked in here!

140
00:07:17,890 --> 00:07:19,910
Rach, he's a friend of ours.

141
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:22,770
You are friends with Dr. Drake Ramoray?

142
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,360
It's hard to be friends with Drake...

143
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:30,280
because of his busy schedule and the fact that he's not real.

144
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:35,200
Hey, or I could bring my keyboard here sometime.

145
00:07:35,450 --> 00:07:36,910
He's coming over.

146
00:07:35,450 --> 00:07:36,910
Joey?

147
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,490
I know. Here, here.

148
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:39,950
Oh.

149
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,960
No. This is my friend Rachel. We went to high school together.

150
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:45,790
Ha, ha, hi.

151
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:45,790
Hi.

152
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,040
I...

153
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:50,710
I love you on that show.

154
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,760
Oh.

155
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,760
I watch you every day.

156
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:55,970
When you took out your kidney to save your ex-wife...

157
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,930
even though she tried to kill you...

158
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,640
It's always nice to meet fans.

159
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,190
She's not crazy, is she?

160
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,190
No.

161
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:08,730
So, uh, how you doing?

162
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,070
Hang on.

163
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:21,660
Hang on. Hang on.

164
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:23,830
Go!

165
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,420
Who's this?

166
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:27,710
Oh, you're gonna like working for me.

167
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:31,800
What's your name? What kind of name is Brindy?

168
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,670
I... Uh, whatever.

169
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,550
Stop talking.

170
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,970
All right, from now on your name is Joan.

171
00:08:39,430 --> 00:08:41,470
You can pick your own last name.

172
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:46,060
Hey, there you are.

173
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:46,060
Uh-oh, it's my boss.

174
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:49,480
All right, here's a list of things for you to do today.

175
00:08:49,650 --> 00:08:51,940
This is gonna be so great. Thank you so much.

176
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:56,360
I gotta go to work. I'm delivering twins, but only one of them is mine.

177
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:05,250
"Drop off my dry cleaning. Pick up my vitamins."

178
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,710
Teach me how to spell vitamins.

179
00:09:09,710 --> 00:09:11,800
"Wear in my new jeans."

180
00:09:13,590 --> 00:09:15,920
You realize what you are, don't you?

181
00:09:13,590 --> 00:09:15,920
What?

182
00:09:16,090 --> 00:09:17,720
You're his bitch.

183
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:21,640
No, no! No!

184
00:09:21,970 --> 00:09:24,430
Wait! You didn't sit on my Kit Kats did you?

185
00:09:24,850 --> 00:09:28,060
No, there was a little, little dip in the market...

186
00:09:28,230 --> 00:09:30,270
and I lost $13 million.

187
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,570
But the Kit Kats are all right?

188
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:36,360
What am I gonna do? I can't call my office, they'll kill me.

189
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:39,700
I can't call my clients, they'll kill themselves!

190
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:42,450
All right, now my chest hurts.

191
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:42,450
What?

192
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,160
My chest hurts. Ugh.

193
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:50,000
Ugh! And now, I can't breathe.

194
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:50,000
Are you having a heart attack?

195
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:53,840
If I were, would I have shooting pains up and down my left arm?

196
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,970
Yes.

197
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,970
Then, yes. That is what I'm having.

198
00:09:57,130 --> 00:09:58,840
Oh, my God!

199
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:06,640
Come on, Pheebs, it's not that bad.

200
00:10:06,810 --> 00:10:10,060
Most people'd be excited if they didn't work for a couple weeks.

201
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:13,270
Most people don't like their jobs. I love my job.

202
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:17,610
I've been not working for three hours, and I'm already going crazy.

203
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:19,400
I miss Joan.

204
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:24,330
Honey, a heart attack is nature's way of telling you to slow down.

205
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:28,410
I always thought it was nature's way of telling you to die. Heh.

206
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,420
You're not gonna die.

207
00:10:31,670 --> 00:10:35,960
I mean, you are going to die, but you're not gonna die today.

208
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:37,420
I wish I was dead.

209
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,340
Let's take a walk.

210
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:44,300
You should consider writing for Talking Out of Your Ass magazine.

211
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:49,560
So what's going on with you?

212
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:54,940
Well, um, I've been doing a lot more of my karate.

213
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:58,900
Still a dry spell with Carol?

214
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:58,900
Yeah.

215
00:10:59,110 --> 00:11:01,610
How long has it been since you've had sex?

216
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:04,910
Well, last weekend...

217
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:04,910
That's not so bad.

218
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:07,870
will be two months...

219
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,000
since I stopped trying.

220
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:14,000
You need to spice things up.

221
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,710
What do you mean?

222
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,710
I don't know.

223
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:19,210
You could tie her up. You could eat stuff off each other.

224
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,510
Oh.

225
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:24,340
Dirty talk, menage a trois, toys.

226
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:24,340
Wow.

227
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:27,720
Role-playing. You're warden, she's prisoner.

228
00:11:27,970 --> 00:11:31,480
You're the pirate, she's the wench.

229
00:11:27,970 --> 00:11:31,480
Okay, I think I got it.

230
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:35,520
You could be two stockbrokers, rolling naked on the trading floor...

231
00:11:35,770 --> 00:11:37,770
and everybody's watching.

232
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,150
It never happened.

233
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:48,950
And over there is Brady's Pub...

234
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,120
where I unwind after a long day of "surgeoning."

235
00:11:52,370 --> 00:11:55,040
Wow! This is so amazing. What else?

236
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:58,340
Well, that is a large piece of television equipment.

237
00:11:58,550 --> 00:12:00,260
And, uh, that is an old man.

238
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,090
Hey, old man!

239
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,090
Hey.

240
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,550
Alrighty. What do you say we head back to my place?

241
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:11,310
Well, wow. Um, you know, I would really love to, but I shouldn't.

242
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:15,810
Why? Why can't the world stop turning?

243
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:20,020
Just for a moment. Just for us.

244
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:23,320
Isn't that a line from the show?

245
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:27,570
Uh, yeah, but, uh...

246
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:30,740
I may have said those things before, but...

247
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:35,210
I never truly meant them until now.

248
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,290
That's a line from the show too!

249
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,090
Okay, you watch too much TV.

250
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,670
Joe, here's the freshly-squeezed orange juice you asked for.

251
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,050
Thanks.

252
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,050
Hi.

253
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,550
Yeah, there's pulp in that.

254
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,850
Yeah?

255
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,850
Heh.

256
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:56,640
I thought we talked about this. I don't like pulp.

257
00:12:56,810 --> 00:13:00,270
No pulp. Pulp isn't juice. All juice. Okay?

258
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:03,570
I'm sorry. I guess I just like the pulp.

259
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:07,280
God, I'm sorry. I am being so rude.

260
00:13:07,450 --> 00:13:10,120
Rachel, would you like a soda or something?

261
00:13:10,370 --> 00:13:14,160
Because Chandler will run right out and get it.

262
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:17,290
Yeah, well, sure, iced tea would be great.

263
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,750
Iced tea.

264
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:24,300
Okay. Anything for you, sir?

265
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:26,970
Did I not just tell him?

266
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:31,390
